  "hindi": "उग्र इन्द्र, जो श्रेष्ठता करने वाला है, दूर से और समीप से हमारे पास सहायता के लिए आए—सबसे बलवानों के साथ, मनुष्यों का स्वामी, वज्र-भुजा वाला, संग्राम में और युद्धों में शत्रुओं को पराजित करने वाला।",
  "english": "May fierce Indra, who makes superiority, come to us from afar and from near for help, with the mightiest ones, the lord of men, vajra-armed, overpowering the hostile ones in the encounter and in battles.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "abhiṣṭi-kṛt 'making superiority' (abhiṣṭi 'superiority, help') is the plain compound sense and is not certain. The two ā ... yāsat are a split preverb (tmesis). ojiṣṭhebhiḥ has no stated noun; rendered 'the mightiest ones'. pṛtanyūn 'hostile ones' (from pṛtanyu, one who makes war).",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
