  "hindi": "इन्द्र हमारे पास भूरे-पीले घोड़ों के साथ आए, हमारी ओर मुख किए हुए, सहायता और उदारता के लिए। वज्रधारी, उदार, प्रचुर इन्द्र हमारे लिए इस यज्ञ के पास खड़ा हो, पुरस्कार की प्राप्ति में।",
  "english": "May Indra come to us with the tawny horses, turned toward us, for help and for bounty. May the wielder of the vajra, the bountiful, the abundant one, stand by this sacrifice for us in the winning of the prize.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "ā ... yātu is a split preverb. tiṣṭhāti (√sthā with anu) is read as a subjunctive 'may he stand by'; the exact form is uncertain. virapśī 'abundant' follows the usual lexicon sense. rādhase is taken as 'for bounty'.",
