  "hindi": "हे इन्द्र, हमारे इस यज्ञ को आगे रखते हुए तुम हमारा संकल्प प्राप्त करोगे। हे वज्रधारी, जुआरी की तरह धनों की प्राप्ति के लिए, तुम्हारे साथ हम शत्रु की होड़ को जीतें।",
  "english": "Placing this sacrifice of ours in front, O Indra, you will win our resolve. Like a gambler, O wielder of the vajra, for the winning of riches, with you may we win the contest of the rival.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "saniṣyasi (√san) is rendered 'you will win'; the object kratum 'resolve' with the verb is uncertain (also 'grant'). aryaḥ is taken as the genitive of ari/arya 'rival, stranger'; it could also be nominative 'lord'. The t in 'vajrin tsanaye' is the edition's regular notation.",
