  "hindi": "हे अपनी शक्ति वाले, अब हमारे समीप, उत्तम मन वाले होकर, भली-भाँति निचोड़े गए सोम की कामना करते हुए— हे इन्द्र, अर्पित मधुर पेय को पियो; पीठ से सम्बन्धित अन्न के साथ आनन्दित हो।",
  "english": "Desiring now, of good mind, near, O possessor of own power, the well-pressed Soma, drink, O Indra, of the offered sweet drink; be exhilarated together with the nourishment belonging to the back.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "uśan nu su naḥ: the relation of naḥ is uncertain (taken 'of us'; could be 'to us'). pṛṣṭhyena is rendered literally 'belonging to the back' (the sense in the rite is not stated). sam ... mamadaḥ is a split preverb; andhasā 'nourishment' (the Soma plant or its drink).",
